  "answer": "Both bugs are clear:\n\n- `src/config.ts` — `enabled` uses `Boolean(value)`, which wrongly coerces `'false'` and `1` to enabled. Only the literal `true` should enable.\n- `src/display.ts` — `display` returns `'ON'` in both branches; disabled features must show `'OFF'`.\n\nI'll fix both while keeping the exact signatures and exports, then run the existing test.\nThe edit tool rejected those parameters; let me retry with the full old/new pair.\n`edit_file` keeps rejecting input, so I'll use `write_file` with the SHA-256 fingerprints from `read_file` instead.\nBoth fixes are in. Now verify with the existing test runner (bun):\nThe test passes. Final state of the fixes:\n\n**`src/config.ts`** — strict enablement:\n```ts\nexport function enabled(value: unknown) { return value === true }\n```\nOnly the literal `true` enables the feature; `false`, `'false'`, `1`, `null`, and `undefined` are all disabled.\n\n**`src/display.ts`** — correct disabled rendering:\n```ts\nexport function display(value: boolean) { return value ? 'ON' : 'OFF' }\n```\nDisabled features now display `OFF` instead of the previous always-`ON` output.\n\nVerification with the existing runner (unchanged):\n```\nbun test v1.3.14\n(pass) strict feature state reaches display\n 1 pass, 0 fail, 6 expect() calls\n```\n\nAll 6 assertions from `test/oracle.test.ts` pass — the five non-`true` values (`false`, `'false'`, `1`, `null`, `undefined`) render `OFF`, and only `enabled(true)` renders `ON`. APIs (function names, signatures, exports) are preserved, and `AGENTS.md`, `package.json`, and `test/oracle.test.ts` were left untouched."
